Eric Gebbett, attempting to repeat his win of last year, went away very fast and at two miles led by fifty yards. However, the other contenders for the title were not to be caught twice running,and at five miles Eric had to relinquish his lead. From this point he fell back steadily and at the finish was seven minutes behind the winner, Clark of Herne Hill. The fact that we could only scrape third place in the team race was mainly due to A.Bishop running some fourteen minutes slower than he did last year.

Result:- 5th, L.C.Bishop 1.55.47; 7th, E.Gebbett 1.58.02;
13th, H.A.Bishop 2.14.13.
